  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nRE-VERIFIED AT TIP, STILL VIOLATED, EXACTLY AS FILED. Production analyze_java on a fixture calling both shapes in one method, dev 11a240f83d:\n\n    Files.write(p, b)        -> java:java.nio.file.Files:0-0:Files.write         cc=None\n    Files.readAllBytes(p)    -> java:java.nio.file.Files:0-0:Files.readAllBytes  cc=None\n    d.exists()               -> java:java.io.File:0-0:exists               cc=method\n    d.mkdirs()               -> java:java.io.File:0-0:mkdirs               cc=method\n\nBoth halves reproduce in the SAME run, which is what makes this a static-vs-instance defect rather than a java-analyzer-wide null: the instance calls are stamped correctly beside the static ones that are not. Note also the static dst name carries the 'Files.' prefix (Files.write) while the instance one does not (exists) -- a second shape difference in the same emission, worth checking before re-keying the catalogue.\n\nThe filing's cautions are unchanged and still apply: measure both directions, and do NOT widen F3 to accept cc=None for method entries."  # 25d5
